# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs.
#
# Without this the context is the whole repository: ~34 MB of captured tapes
# under data/, the git history, the C++ build trees and the model checkpoints —
# none of which any COPY in the Dockerfile references. The daemon still has to
# receive and hash all of it before the first instruction runs.
#
# This is not the same list as .gitignore. Several things committed to git are
# still useless in the image (notebooks, docs, the C++ sources), and one thing
# git ignores is essential (nothing, currently — the replay tapes and the ONNX
# graph are both committed on purpose).

.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Captured data. The demo runs on the committed replay tapes under
# notebooks/sample_data/, which the Dockerfile copies by name.
data/
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.pth

# Everything under inference_cpp is a separate artefact with its own build; the
# serving image runs the ONNX graph, not the hand-written C++ path.
inference_cpp/

# Research surface. The image serves the RESULTS in benchmarks/*.json, not the
# notebooks that produced them.
notebooks/*.ipynb
notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints/
docs/
*.md
!serving/*.md

# Benchmark artefacts that are not JSON records.
benchmarks/*.png
benchmarks/*.csv
benchmarks/*.py

# Python and tooling noise.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/
tests/
run_checks.sh
